{"source": {"title": "静夜思", "author": "李白", "text": "床前明月光，疑是地上霜。
举头望明月，低头思故乡。"}, "translation": "Before my bed the bright moonlight falls,
I take it for frost upon the ground.
I raise my head and gaze at the bright moon;
I lower it, and think of home."}

{"source": {"title": "浣溪沙·一曲新词酒一杯", "author": "晏殊", "text": "一曲新词酒一杯，去年天气旧亭台。夕阳西下几时回？
无可奈何花落去，似曾相识燕归来。小园香径独徘徊。"}, "translation": "One new song, one cup of wine;
last year's weather, the old pavilion and terrace.
The sun sets in the west — when will it return?

Helplessly the flowers fall away;
seemingly familiar, the swallows come back.
Alone I pace the fragrant path of the small garden."}

{"source": {"title": "登高", "author": "杜甫", "text": "风急天高猿啸哀，渚清沙白鸟飞回。
无边落木萧萧下，不尽长江滚滚来。
万里悲秋常作客，百年多病独登台。
艰难苦恨繁霜鬓，潦倒新停浊酒杯。"}, "translation": "Fierce wind, high sky, the gibbons' mournful cry;
Clear sandbar, white sand, birds wheel and fly.
Boundless, the falling leaves come rustling down;
Endless, the Yangtze rolls and surges toward me.
Ten thousand miles away, in autumn grief, ever a stranger;
A hundred years of sickness, alone I climb the terrace.
Hardship and bitter grief have thickened frost at my temples;
Worn out, I have of late set down my cup of turbid wine."}

{"source": {"title": "送元二使安西", "author": "王维", "text": "渭城朝雨浥轻尘，客舍青青柳色新。
劝君更尽一杯酒，西出阳关无故人。"}, "translation": "Morning rain at Weicheng dampens the fine dust;
The guest house green, the willows newly bright.
Drink yet one more cup of wine, I urge you—
West of Yang Pass, no old friends remain."}
